---
import Site from '../layouts/Site.astro';
const isPreview = import.meta.env.LFNYC_PRODUCTION_BUILD !== 'approved';
---

<Site
  title="Website terms"
  description="This Little Fight NYC website explains services and prepares messages. Paid work begins only under an agreed written scope."
>
  <article class="policy shell">
    <nav class="breadcrumb" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
      <a href="/">Home</a>
      <span aria-hidden="true">/</span>
      <span>Website terms</span>
    </nav>
    <p class="label">Updated October 9, 2026</p>
    <h1>A CLEAR START.</h1>
    <p>
      {isPreview
        ? 'This is a design preview of a Little Fight NYC service website, available for review.'
        : 'This Little Fight NYC website explains our services.'}{' '}
      It does not take payments, place orders or create a service agreement.
    </p>
    <h2>Before paid work</h2>
    <p>
      Consulting is free. A written scope sets the work, price, timing, access
      requirements and responsibilities before paid work begins. Website
      descriptions do not replace that agreement.
    </p>
    <h2>Timing</h2>
    <p>
      The callback target is within two hours, 9am to 9pm Eastern. It is not a
      guarantee that a repair will finish in two hours. A qualifying website
      scope may include a written 14-day promise with eligibility, starting
      conditions, responsibilities and remedy stated in the scope.
    </p>
    <h2>Your accounts and work</h2>
    <p>
      Clients own their code, data, domain, hosting and documentation. Specific
      deliverables and any third-party licenses belong in the written scope.
    </p>
    <h2>Public examples</h2>
    <p>
      Portfolio screenshots show publicly available client websites on the
      recorded capture date. Client names, photographs, artwork and other
      materials retain their original ownership. These examples describe website
      work, not measured increases in bookings, traffic or revenue.
    </p>
    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>
      Write to{' '}
      <a href="mailto:hello@littlefightnyc.com">hello@littlefightnyc.com</a> for
      current service details.
    </p>
  </article>
</Site>
